<title>USA: U.S. farm trade surplus $2.060 billion in January.</title>
<headline>U.S. farm trade surplus $2.060 billion in January.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. trade surplus in agricultural commodities was $2.060 billion in January, down from $2.306 billion in December, the Commerce Department said Thursday.</p>
<p>In its monthly trade report, Commerce pegged farm exports at $4.901 billion in December, down $5.164 billion in December. Imports were $2.841 billion, compared to $2.858 billion the previous month.</p>
</text>
